Subject: [PATCH] mc: kill order healers before elites, re-taunt after teleport

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Majordomo Executus's eight adds are four Flamewaker Healers (11663) and
four Flamewaker Elites (11664). The `moltencore` strategy sets no kill
order, so the party does not burn the healers first. Teleport Target
(20534) throws the tank into the fire pit every 30 seconds (first at
15 seconds), dropping threat on the adds it held, and nothing re-taunts
them afterwards.

While a Flamewaker healer is alive, elites are excluded from DPS/attacker
target selection so the party burns the healers (the skull target) first
and the elites after. When Teleport Target clears and the tank is back,
a MajordomoReTauntMultiplier prioritizes attack/melee on the held adds so
the tank re-establishes threat.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream adds a Majordomo kill order and a post-teleport re-taunt to the
Molten Core combat strategy, at which point this patch is redundant.

APPLIES TO

    mod-playerbots @ 60e6555e4e4b552ee4c6551b466aff648916f38b
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCHelpers.h, MoltenCoreNPCs and MoltenCoreSpells
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCMultipliers.h, MajordomoReTauntMultiplier
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCMultipliers.cpp, MajordomoReTauntMultiplier::GetValue
    src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp, RaidMcStrategy::InitMultipliers and
    RaidMcStrategy::AppendTargetExclusions

Uses only members already present at this pin: `PlayerbotAI::IsTank`,
`AttackAction`, `MeleeAction`, `AI_VALUE(Unit*, "current target")`,
`Unit::GetEntry`, `Unit::HasAura`, `AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers")`.

